Hi Marwan,

I think the issue might be that nimble uses the precision as the default parameter of `dnorm`, following historical precedent of BUGS and JAGS.
So you may be specifying overly precise priors for `alpha[1]` and `alpha[2]`.

To use standard deviation as the parameter, you can do:

x ~ dnorm(0, sd = 10)

-chris

